# Win32 & Windows Systems Engineering

This skill standardizes low-level Windows native programming, Win32 API subsystems, Windows Services, Registry automation, and crash dump analysis.

---

## 🪟 Core Focus Areas

1. **Win32 Handles & Concurrency:** Kernel objects (`HANDLE`), synchronization primitives (Mutex, Semaphore, Event, `WaitForSingleObject`, `WaitForMultipleObjects`).
2. **Windows Registry:** Native registry APIs (`RegOpenKeyEx`, `RegSetValueEx`, `RegQueryValueEx`) and safe `.reg` script generation.
3. **Windows Services Architecture:** Service Control Manager (SCM), `StartServiceCtrlDispatcher`, `ServiceMain`, and `SetServiceStatus`.
4. **Structured Exception Handling (SEH) & Minidumps:** `__try / __except`, Vectored Exception Handling (VEH), `MiniDumpWriteDump`, and WinDbg crash dump triage.
5. **Application Manifests (`app.manifest`):** Per-Monitor DPI V2 awareness, UAC elevation execution levels (`asInvoker` vs `requireAdministrator`), and UTF-8 code page support.

---

## ⚙️ 1. Windows Application Manifest (`app.manifest`)

Always embed a modern application manifest to avoid legacy Windows DPI scaling blur and execution quirks:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<assembly manifestVersion="1.0" xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">
  <assemblyIdentity version="1.0.0.0" name="MyWin32App.app"/>
  <trustInfo xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v2">
    <security>
      <requestedPrivileges xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
        <requestedExecutionLevel level="asInvoker" uiAccess="false" />
      </requestedPrivileges>
    </security>
  </trustInfo>
  <compatibility xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:compatibility.v1">
    <application>
      <!-- Windows 10 and 11 -->
      <supportedOS Id="{8e0f7a12-bfb3-4fe8-b9a5-48fd50a15a9a}" />
    </application>
  </compatibility>
  <application xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
    <windowsSettings>
      <dpiAwareness xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2016/WindowsSettings">PerMonitorV2, PerMonitor</dpiAwareness>
      <activeCodePage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2019/WindowsSettings">UTF-8</activeCodePage>
    </windowsSettings>
  </application>
</assembly>
```

